      "title": "The Soviet Union breaks apart",
      "description": "Gorbachev resigns as Soviet president. Independent states take the place of the union.",
      "source_ids": ["soviet-collapse"]
    },
    {
      "month": "1993-04",
      "title": "Web software becomes free to use",
      "description": "CERN releases its World Wide Web software into the public domain, helping others build on it.",
      "source_ids": ["web-release"]
    }
  ],
  "what_happened_next": {
    "text": "Coca-Cola led these choices over five years. Exxon and the US basket gained less, while Sony and international shares rose only modestly. Buying a film studio was a dramatic story, but it did not make Sony the best investment here. These results belong to this particular starting date and window, not a rule about whole industries.",
