      "web-release"
    ]
  },
  "reflection": {
    "what_people_were_focused_on": "The Berlin Wall had opened, financial oversight was under scrutiny, and Sony was expanding into Hollywood.",
    "what_actually_mattered": "Returns depended on the full investment path, not the size of a headline. A large acquisition was a business decision whose investment result still had to unfold.",
    "what_faded_away": "The excitement of a Hollywood deal did not tell you the eventual winner. A widely reported event was not the same as a useful price forecast.",
    "what_nobody_knew": "The web’s growth and the Soviet Union’s breakup were still ahead. Even with that history revealed, the exact investment ranking would have been hard to predict.",
